Quick Powershell commands to search for files 

Test-Path "C:\Path\To\filename.exe"    -----> True/False
Get-Item "C:\ProgramData\filename.exe" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue  ------> If exist then results if not then File does not exist: - No output

Get-ChildItem "C:\ProgramData" -Filter "filename.exe" -File -Recurse -Depth 2 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue     ------> checks 2 level sub folders

Get-ChildItem "C:\Users\*\Downloads" -Filter "filename.exe" -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

Get-ChildItem "C:\Program Files\WindowsApps" -Filter "*WhatsApp*" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue   --------> for Windows Apps
